const rec1 = "STAGE: review all three proposals against the frozen evidence bundle cf0a8c8be17804d3 / 735c028526119499 / 7b70423833611cca.
GOAL: ground each placement in the shared evidence, then rank 1..3.
READ: E5 (successor-entropy stratification), E6 (width-20 beam survival + depth 1/2/3/4 gold-prefix survival + recall@10), E7 (teacher-forced per-position NLL), E8/E9 (cohort/profile signal), E10/E11 (transition graph stats: 115582 distinct edges, density 5.3266, mean out-degree 5.4526; same_first_prefix_rate 0.0907), E12/E13 (Poincare/Gromov curved ops, post-Stage-2 SID construction).
OBSERVED: E6/E7 localise the failure at the deepest token. l1_br: depth4 survival 0.068, beams 0.0678, T4 NLL 9.03, recall 0.04671. l1_br_euclid/l1_only: depth4 0.085/0.086, beams 0.0847/0.0855, T4 NLL 1.23/1.19, recall 0.06207/0.06233. Best probe is resample 0.06363 (beams 0.0884, depth4 0.088). Hyperbolic successor variants underperform: successor_geodesic_coarse 0.05500, _v2 0.05463, tangent_successor_residual 0.05500. E10 shows a cyclic, non-tree transition graph (density 5.33).
REASONING: all three edit only the deepest level, which the evidence supports. HORO-TRANSPLANT-L is the most conservative and best-matched to the diagnosed locus: no new codes, vocabulary size unchanged, a constant-free sign gate Delta_i<=0 tied to the frozen Stage-2 child anchors that Stage 3 actually reads, one synchronous pass. gromovcrit-deepest-split is precise (one-Poisson-sigma confusion band is derived, margin rule M1>M0 directly targets the previous round's coverage-first failure) but stacks C1,C2,S-a,S-b,S-c,M1 and splits codes, so its own stated risk is an empty critical set; still better grounded than GROMOV4 because it fixes kappa=-1 so the geometry cannot degenerate. GROMOV4-MARGIN-GATE sets c=1/max(delta_G,1) from a transition graph that E10 shows is dense/cyclic, so delta_G is likely large and the geometry collapses to near-Euclidean, plus five simultaneous gates and a Stage-2 cell-size cap invite inertness.
OPEN: none; ranking fixed.
";
await tools.progress.append_progress({ content: rec1 });
return "recorded";

const final = "FINAL ANSWER (complete, self-contained):
RANK: HORO-TRANSPLANT-L | position=1 | reason=E6/E7 pin the loss at the deepest position (l1_br T4 NLL 9.03, depth-4 prefix survival 0.068, recall 0.04671 vs l1_only 0.06233) and this proposal changes only k_L with no new codes and a constant-free Delta_i<=0 gate against the frozen Stage-2 child anchors, so it is the least invasive and most directly coupled to the token Stage 3 must emit; E6 also shows heavy hyperbolic successor machinery underperforming (successor_geodesic_coarse 0.05500), favouring its minimal one-pass form.
RANK: gromovcrit-deepest-split | position=2 | reason=E5's successor-entropy spread (top1 mass 0.4375 low-entropy vs 0.0543 high-entropy quintile) makes a per-prefix top-two confusion table a grounded precision condition, and E6/E7 justify editing level L only, but its C1/C2/S-a/S-b/S-c/M1 stack plus code splitting carries the proposal's own empty-critical-set risk, so it is placed below the simpler transplant; still ranked above GROMOV4 because kappa=-1 keeps the geometry genuinely curved.
RANK: GROMOV4-MARGIN-GATE-SID | position=3 | reason=E10/E11 show a cyclic transition graph (115582 edges, density 5.3266, mean out-degree 5.4526), so the measured delta_G in c=1/max(delta_G,1) is likely large and the curvature near zero, making the geometry effectively Euclidean and weakening the coupling; E6/E7 also show the deepest token is the right locus, but the five simultaneous gates and the frozen Stage-2 cell-size cap make an inert move set likely, so it is placed last.
";
await tools.progress.append_progress({ content: final });
return "final recorded";
